 # T-102 Connect the GitHub and Jira MCP servers
 Product wants the agent to read GitHub issues and Jira tickets through the company's MCP servers. Read-only. Keep tokens per user.
+
+## Evidence
+Status: implemented locally; not verified against the real servers.
+- Specialist: adk-agent-interoperability (consume MCP), supporting adk-tool-auth-and-secrets and adk-agent-security.
+- `support_agent/mcp_config.py`: URLs, read-only `tool_filter` allowlists, timeouts, cache TTL, per-user `header_provider` (fails closed when the token is missing).
+- `support_agent/agent.py`: `github_toolset` and `jira_toolset` (Streamable HTTP, prefixes `github`/`jira`) on a new read-only `issue_tracker_agent`, added to `root_agent.sub_agents`.
+- `support_agent/__init__.py`: `root_agent` now imported lazily, so the tests can import the package without google.adk.
+- Local: `tests/test_mcp_config.py` passed 5/5 on Python 3.11 (direct runner); `pytest tests` on Python 3.9: 6 passed, 1 skipped.
+- Not run: `tests/test_agent_mcp.py` (needs google-adk 2.8.0), `mcp_tool_inventory.py` against both servers (remote, needs owner approval), fake-server tests, a live tools/list and read-only tools/call.
+- Open: confirm tool names against the servers' tools/list and commit `mcp-manifest.json`; confirm each token was issued for its MCP server's audience.
